  Warnings:
  - Whole Building stitched 4 near-matching modular seam edge(s) within 0,125 source
    units so fracture pieces can cross authored segment boundaries.
  - Whole Building Hollow Shell added Wall Thickness to 3 open surface component(s)
    and preserved the authored thickness of 0 closed volumetric component(s).
  - 'Shell breakdown (triangles, volume, watertight): #1 16 tri, vol 141,257, OPEN;
    #2 4 tri, vol 180,427, OPEN; #3 4 tri, vol 847,094, OPEN'
  - "Source has 3 separate mesh shells (0 closed, 3 found before preparation). Per-shell
    fracture: OFF (shells fracture merged) \u2014 classified as one hollow shell
    (an inner surface faces inward)."
  - Kept 6 nested surface islands together as one hollow shell. Auto Axis and every
    fracture plane are shared by the outer and inner walls so generated caps connect
    them instead of closing the cavity separately.
  - Fragment volume sum is 176% of the source volume. The source mesh is probably
    open or self-intersecting; caps were approximated.
  - Concrete fracture safely exported 245 of the configured maximum of 250. The remaining
    candidates would create an open boundary, an extreme needle or an invalid micro-fragment
    merge, so they were not exported.
  - 41 cut segment(s) could not be chained within the normal weld tolerance; affected
    caps preserved their real edge order and closed the final numerical seam.
  - Intact collision uses 4 compound parts. In Whole Building modular workflow each
    authored panel keeps its own Hollow Shell collider instead of one convex hull
    spanning the room interior.
  - 4 rectangular modular wall/floor collider(s) use oriented BoxColliders with the
    authored Hollow Shell thickness. No triangulated collider surface is stored for
    those panels; irregular modules keep the convex-mesh fallback.
  - Whole Building combined 8 coplanar modular panel seam(s) into continuous wall/floor
    colliders and support groups. Corners and real gaps remain separate.
  - 'Large Whole Building defers inactive fragment physics: only pieces that actually
    detach receive a Rigidbody. This keeps a local first break from registering all
    245 pieces with PhysX.'
